It is Wednesday afternoon after work.
I walk to the repair shop on my street.
I am picking up my bicycle.
The mechanic sees me.
He says: "Hello Frau Flores, your bicycle is ready."
I answer: "Good afternoon, that is great."
He brings my bicycle to me.
He says: "The brakes are working perfectly again."
I test the brakes.
They are really very good.
I say: "Thank you very much!"
I push my bicycle onto the pavement.
I take the U-Bahn to the office every day.
But now I will sometimes ride the bicycle.
The office is not too far away.
It is now exactly half past five.
I am meeting Frau Krüger at six o'clock.
So I still have a little time.
